WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:05.205
[Todd Field] <i> Long before steroids
and multi-million dollar contracts,</i>

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.508
<i>there was a truly independent ball club,</i>

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:12.645
<i>a bunch of guys who were hopeless dreamers
looking for a second chance.</i>

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.280
<i>In short...</i>

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.217
the best kind of people.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.220
[Carren Woods] <i> When we first heard
about Bing Russell,</i>

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.522
<i>there was this buzz about,
"Well, who's Bing Russell?"</i>

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.290
[Field] <i> And he was in
The Magnificent Seven</i>

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.159
<i>and he's the sheriff on</i>  Bonanza.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:30.096
My dad got killed 126 times,
I think it was.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.501
[Field] <i> Why would Bing Russell
come to Portland?</i>

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.304
Bing was out to prove that
independent baseball could work.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.640
[Bob Richmond] <i> And I think we charged Bing
$500 for the franchise.</i>

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.375
[Kurt Russell] <i> So we started from scratch.</i>

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.444
<i>"We're going to have open tryouts."</i>

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.680
"Show us for the fools that we are
coming from Hollywood."

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.317
[Frank Peters] <i> You'd expect maybe
40 or 50 people to show up,</i>

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.253
and I think 300 showed up.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.555
[Woods] <i> Guys who drove
clear across the country</i>

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.557
<i>and sacrificed this or sold this</i>

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.626
<i>just for the chance
to come and try out for the team.</i>

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.629
I don't care about the money.
I just want to play ball.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.698
[Field] <i> There was no press handlers.</i>

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.067
<i>There was no groomed image.</i>

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:11.004
<i>There were just these furry, hairy, funny,
great bunch of guys...</i>

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.272
[bat cracking]

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.308
<i>...and the things that happened
on the field were absolutely insane.</i>

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.576
[bat cracking]

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.578
[Woods] <i> Organized baseball
didn't like Bing</i>

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:22.282
<i>and they did everything they could
to make sure Bing didn't win.</i>

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.516
[bat cracking]

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.784
[Kurt] <i> He couldn't stand them.</i>

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.453
They couldn't stand him.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.390
Portland is the greatest
baseball city in the world.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:33.760
[Field] <i> We broke attendance records
in the entire Minor Leagues that year.</i>

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.330
[Rob Nelson] <i> We really emphasized fun.</i>

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.731
[Richmond] <i> The fans loved it.</i>

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.267
[Field] <i> I've never seen a ball team</i>

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.771
<i>and fans behave the way
they did with the Mavericks.</i>

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.675
[Kurt] <i> He created the most successful team
in the history of Minor League Baseball.</i>

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.547
[bat cracking]

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.051
"This is gonna be magic."

